{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Taxonomy is completely unwired from execution and recovery\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/engine.py\",\"line\":418,\"severity\":\"critical\",\"claim\":\"The engine retries every non-successful, non-cancelled ExecutionResult directly and never imports or calls FailureClassifierChain, scheduler_action, HoldRegistry, or boot_sweep. RecoveryManager likewise marks runs CRASHED directly.\",\"scenario\":\"A CLI rate-limit response exits 1 with a rate-limit message. The engine retries it up to the generic cap, records FAILED, and never creates a durable park hold; Directive 9's end-to-end rate-limit and reconcile behavior is therefore absent in production.\"},{\"title\":\"Retry-After is discarded and malformed numeric resets can wedge or reopen a credential\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/failures.py\",\"line\":239,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"The structured classifier reads only absolute reset_at/retry_after_epoch, silently ignores a Retry-After delay, accepts bool/NaN/infinity as numeric reset values, and does not validate that a reset is a finite absolute epoch.\",\"scenario\":\"A provider reports structured {'rate_limited': true, 'retry_after': 60}; classification produces reset_at=null, so the ACCOUNT hold never auto-expires. Conversely reset_at=true becomes 1.0 and reopens immediately, while NaN never satisfies now >= reset_at and wedges the credential indefinitely.\"},{\"title\":\"Reconcile can select an earlier ACCOUNT hold and reopen a known-shut window\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/failures.py\",\"line\":378,\"severity\":\"critical\",\"claim\":\"For competing holds with the same scope, reconcile retains the first iterable record rather than the most restrictive/latest reset. placed_at is ignored.\",\"scenario\":\"Durable records for one credential contain ACCOUNT reset_at=100 followed by a later ACCOUNT reset_at=1000. Reconcile keeps 100; at now=150 admits() returns true even though the later durable rate-limit record says the account remains shut. Ordering records oppositely changes the outcome.\"},{\"title\":\"PROBE holds authorize every caller claiming to be a resume\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/failures.py\",\"line\":384,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"A PROBE hold has no probe/run identity, and admits trusts an unconstrained boolean is_resume. It cannot enforce the stated invariant that only the probing resume is admitted.\",\"scenario\":\"After one parked run is selected as the probe, several queued resumed runs call admits(credential, now, is_resume=True). Every one is admitted concurrently, producing the stampede PROBE was intended to prevent.\"},{\"title\":\"FailureSignal has no runtime type validation, so booleans can route failures as success\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/failures.py\",\"line\":224,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"Dataclass annotations do not enforce types; Python bool is an int. structured_outcome_classifier therefore treats exit_code=False as exit code zero, and truthy non-booleans for timed_out/cancelled also alter routing.\",\"scenario\":\"A decoded adapter payload supplies exit_code=false for a failed process. FailureSignal accepts it and the classifier returns PASS at structured grade, bypassing retries, parking, escalation, and failure recording.\"},{\"title\":\"boot_sweep does not inspect run state and can re-adopt terminal work\",\"file\":\"src/gnosis/kernel/failures.py\",\"line\":461,\"severity\":\"major\",\"claim\":\"StrandedRun.state is never read. boot_sweep applies recovery dispositions to every supplied record, including completed or otherwise terminal runs.\",\"scenario\":\"A startup caller supplies durable runs without perfectly prefiltering them and includes a SUCCEEDED run whose old process is absent. The sweep defaults it to AGENT_CRASH and READOPTED, allowing already completed work to be executed again.\"}],\"overall\":\"FAIL: the unit contains several useful isolated primitives, but its production paths are not connected to the engine, retry loop, or recovery manager, so Directive 9 is not implemented end-to-end; independently, reset parsing, competing-hold reconciliation, probe admission, and unchecked runtime coercions can cause premature reopening, permanent credential wedges, stampedes, or incorrect success routing.\"}"}}
